# The legend rule (CR 704.5j): Bot1 casts a second Ajani, Nacatl Pariah on turn 3, with the first still out, and is asked
# which to keep. The older one is chosen, so the one that stays is no longer summoning sick, and the newer goes to the
# graveyard, not destroyed. Both Ajanis' enters triggers still make their Cat Warrior, one each.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains x2
Mox Pearl
Ajani, Nacatl Pariah x2
Plains x3
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ajani, Nacatl Pariah.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ajani, Nacatl Pariah.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ajani, Nacatl Pariah#1)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Ajani, Nacatl Pariah
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains; Plains; Mox Pearl; Ajani, Nacatl Pariah; Cat Warrior Token; Cat Warrior Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Ajani, Nacatl Pariah.SummoningSick = false
